== Executable repair and theorem

`round3/validate.py` first enforces the selected Request classes and Grouping
None. The supported schema is declared independently of mutable anchors from
the actual producer paths/types: known object fields, exact scalar kinds,
positional two-element edge tuples, numeric routing-map keys. Python boolean is
not an integer. Unknown expression/interface fields outside exact owner paths
reject. This is a finite supported-shape contract, not a universal JSON theorem.

It compares full graph keys with multiplicity, IDs, order, all nontransformed
diagram/payload fields, positional vertex/edge incidence, routing, physical
counts, interaction and particle metadata, automorphism/basis/factors, and typed
flags. Owner domains are symmetric and unique before either side is indexed;
missing/extra owners reject explicitly. Only exact documented expression and
interface paths admit the five audited whole-symbol mappings and checked named
port transports. Model/request/options/grouping comparisons are type-strict.

Every live decoded expression links to its exact payload path. Current raw
expressions also link; historical raw expressions remain observed producer
associations. Singleton master/member/source/name/factor/ratio records are
checked. Complete per-symbol attribute/tag definitions must be internally
consistent and identical across routes, including interfaces, before parsing in
Symbolica. No registration inheritance supplies missing semantics.

Every distinct supported mapped decoded text, including literal-only projectors
and ports, is parsed under both kernels and compared with its token-tree render.
The additive fresh formal witness avoids the retained helper's unit-power
safeguard limitation: equality of A+z and B+z entails A=B by exact cancellation.
It is not a physical parameter or numerical sample. Raw text is preserved for
this parser-faithfulness check, so a leading-space ` real` attribute cannot be
silently repaired by the token renderer. Unsupported/trailing syntax rejects.

The precise result is #emph[Symbolica-normalized local/global equality under
identical attribute-bearing definitions]. CT/YM nonliteral pairs are even cyclic
rotations of antisymmetric `spenso::f`, bound to the actual immutable definition
sources. Nonliteral comparisons use both orders in fresh processes under both
kernels. Every graph also checks its prefactor times complete local factors
against its aggregate, within each producer. Sums stay whole; no whole-graph
distribution, trace, expansion or parameter substitution is used.

Frozen capture anchors are a separate, subsequent provenance layer. Baseline
anchor pairs are self-comparisons, not additional algebra or cross-route proof.
Matched-anchor controls isolate semantic predicates by changing consumed inputs
and corresponding anchors together. Separately, model changes shared across
routes but not anchors exercise anchor identity. No hash/FNV determines semantic
equality.

Physical graph construction, source factors and historical decoding are still
source-qualified capture facts. Their full cross-route equality is checked;
this does not independently derive a general physics theorem from graph data.

