== Evidence, reproduction and reporting limits

The round-three receipt and inventory bind consumed inputs, emitted pair files,
ELFs, validator/helper source, source revisions, compiler/features, actual argv,
safe environment policy, times, exits and result hashes. Relied-on inputs and
ELFs are hashed before and after final credited runs. Whole frozen historical
and current evidence/reviews are rehashed before/after. Old executions do not
gain retroactive pre-run hashes or transcripts: A's independent post-run checks
are separately attributed. All new diagnostic top-level execution commands have
recorded command files; interactive source-edit/read operations are not claimed
as an exhaustive shell transcript.

No producer or checker is rebuilt here. Original `build-final.log` files are
preserved pre-decoding build logs, not final credited ELF build logs. Successful
pre-decoding attempt1 runs are not failures; a later license-aborted attempt has
no retained log. Round-two development roots `oracle-numerator-family-round2`
and `oracle-numerator-family-round2-final` are superseded; only
`oracle-numerator-family-round2-candidate` was credited there. A's fingerprint
qualification covers 336 historical and 341 current Cargo units, with actual
per-unit feature/profile limits; root default/native is not the full dependency
closure and test/build root profiles differ. Cache metadata corroborates identity,
not original build command logs.

Archived diagnostic Rust bytes remain unchanged and outside ordinary Cargo
target discovery, avoiding their unused-import all-target lint exposure. They
still match Nix's common `*.rs` source selection, so Cargo exclusion is not Nix
source-filter exclusion and can affect source/cache identity. A reproducible
observational overlay must start in a #emph[new private copy/workspace] at the
exact source base and apply the retained diagnostic patch there. Never restore
diagnostics into frozen task @, historical holder or other lanes.

Only direct runtime ELFs receive a private license. No new Nix subprocess is
needed in this correction. Any Nix invocation must unset both license variables;
old unrecorded Nix/license assertions are not upgraded to recorded evidence.
No secrets, secret hashes, store deletion or policy changes are involved.

Both old notes now have superseded registry entries with exact titles, unique
IDs/sources and one current certificate owner. Scoped canonical checks and
pinned PDF/semantic HTML are recorded. The full docs builder is not green:
its eight inherited HTML source violations are #emph[first-gate observations],
